WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.610
Last time on True Fear I told you about my
creepy experiences with The Hobo King.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.290
If you haven’t seen that episode, I’ll
leave a link so you can go see it.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.830
I’ve also been talking with more people
who used to live at that building who saw

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:20.261
my Hobo King video, and I’ve come across
some new information and horror stories, so

00:00:20.261 --> 00:00:26.660
if you’d like to see a Part II to that video,
leave a like and let me know in the comments.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:30.630
So we basically had to flee the apartment,
as it became unlivable due to the bugs.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.960
They were supposed to treat our apartment
right away, but they cared about money a lot

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:39.110
more than the well being of their tenants,
and that’s today’s horror story.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:43.600
No, but when that happened we found ourselves
hotel hopping for a while.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:48.170
As I mentioned in episode 2, it was student
housing, so the school would put us up in

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:49.190
nearby hotels.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:52.980
I know this sounds cool, like some awesome
Zac and Cody stuff, but the apartment complex

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:57.150
manager kept lying about when they would actually
be treating our apartment, so the school kept

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:59.360
putting us in hotels for one day at a time.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:03.140
And different hotels would fill up on different
days, so we had to move to a different hotel

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.110
almost every night, and it just got to the
point where it was exhausting.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:09.120
Couple that with the fact that we were in
classes and had our own lives to deal with

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:13.580
and had to constantly fight with the apartment
management to get our unit fixed and the hotel

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.080
thing wasn’t a whole lot of fun.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.200
It was also kind of a health detriment.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.890
We didn’t have a kitchen to cook in, nor
did we have any place we could store food,

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:23.370
so we had to go out and get fast food all
of the time.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:30.100
That’s where this story begins, at an Extended
Stay America in Woodland Hills, CA.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.970
So I had gotten out of class and checked into
the hotel.

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:36.900
I was feeling pretty hungry so I decide to
go out and find somewhere I could get food.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.710
In the hotel, there are all these super-long
hallways, and our room was at the end of the

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:41.710
last hallway.

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:45.300
So I’m headed out of there and I see this
door partially open at the end of one of the

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.000
halls, and this older woman standing in the
dark.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.470
So I think, “Oh she must be getting ready
to go out and leave her room.”

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:55.210
Well, turns out I was right… in a way.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:59.970
Once I get closer she walks out of the room
and she’s standing in the hallway.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:03.830
It seems as if she’s looking at me, but
when I saw her eyes, it was more like she

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:07.330
was looking past me or looking through me
or something.

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:10.819
Like her head was pointed in my direction,
but it was almost like she didn’t see me

00:02:10.819 --> 00:02:15.630
at all, she was in her own world, and in this
world of hers there was a ghost standing just

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:16.630
past where I was.

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:20.230
I know this hard to picture, but that’s
the best way I can describe it.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:24.629
So that was unsettling, but not as unsettling
as what would come next.

00:02:24.629 --> 00:02:25.719
The voice.

00:02:25.719 --> 00:02:28.439
It was like something straight out of a horror
movie.

00:02:28.439 --> 00:02:30.379
And what she said didn’t make it any better.

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:34.159
Now I don’t remember her exact words, so
I’m just paraphrasing.

00:02:34.159 --> 00:02:37.700
It was something along the lines of “Why
hello Gerald!

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:41.349
Won’t you come in and have some supper;
make you some supper.”

00:02:41.349 --> 00:02:43.959
And then... she actually started laughing.

00:02:43.959 --> 00:02:47.219
And meanwhile I just didn’t even think about
responding to any of this.

00:02:47.219 --> 00:02:49.390
I just kept walking and never looked back.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.859
She kept talking as I walked away but I didn’t
hear her.

00:02:51.859 --> 00:02:56.730
So yeah, that was one of the creepier things
I’d ever seen, but I guess it could have

00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:00.969
been like a prank or maybe she had a bluetooth
I didn’t see or something.

00:03:00.969 --> 00:03:05.340
I was honestly just trying to come up with
an excuse for my own comfort at that point.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:08.489
But after that I went out, got some food and
came back.

00:03:08.489 --> 00:03:13.059
And at that point I had pretty much forgotten
about it all, but then I turn into that hallway

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:15.829
again, and what do I see?

00:03:15.829 --> 00:03:20.120
In the same exact spot where the woman wandered
out to before, there was a police officer

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:24.670
taking down some notes and the door that the
woman came out of was open and the place was

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.150
cleared out.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:30.949
I never found out what happened that night
while I was out getting food, but I still

00:03:30.949 --> 00:03:34.560
do wonder if I had just been lucky to have
not been a victim.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:39.030
Clearly SOMETHING went down while I was gone
and it was big enough to get the cops called

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.529
and start an investigation.

00:03:40.529 --> 00:03:43.750
What stuck with me more than anything was
the look in that woman’s eye.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.939
She just looked so hollow.

00:03:45.939 --> 00:03:49.500
After thinking more about the situation, I
came up with the theory that she was having

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.939
some kind of flashback in her head.

00:03:51.939 --> 00:03:53.629
Possibly a trauma induced reaction.

00:03:53.629 --> 00:03:54.819
What led me to this theory?

00:03:54.819 --> 00:03:58.519
Well, first I wanted to analyse why she was
even staying at this hotel.

00:03:58.519 --> 00:04:00.459
This isn’t in like a touristy part of LA.

00:04:00.459 --> 00:04:05.169
It’s at least 30 minutes away from the beach,
30 minutes away from Universal, and 45 minutes

00:04:05.169 --> 00:04:06.279
away from Hollywood.

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:11.480
So that left me with two likely possibilities:
she’s visiting family, or there’s something

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.700
wrong at home, causing her to have to stay
in the hotel -- the same reason I was technically

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:16.700
staying there.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:20.980
Based on her behaviour, I’ve decided to
explore the latter, as that seems more likely

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:21.980
to me.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:26.289
We have very little to go off of in this situation,
really just what she said, which, unfortunately

00:04:26.289 --> 00:04:29.120
I don’t remember all of it perfectly word
for word.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.389
This was before I started doing True Fear,
so I didn’t think to write it down or anything.

00:04:33.389 --> 00:04:37.410
But I think her dialogue does offer some possible
clues as to what was going on.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:41.699
So first, there was this character Gerald
who she seemed to be talking to.

00:04:41.699 --> 00:04:45.289
Based on the way that she was talking to him
and the fact that she asked him to come in

00:04:45.289 --> 00:04:49.669
for supper, Gerald may have been her husband,
or possibly a her son.

00:04:49.669 --> 00:04:54.110
At the beginning of the interaction, she seems
kind of surprised to see Gerald, so I took

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:59.370
this as they had been apart for some time
and she was now day dreaming or hallucinating

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:00.560
about seeing him again.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.449
That’s why I think that this may have been
trauma related in some way.

00:05:03.449 --> 00:05:07.940
For example, if Gerald was her husband, I
get the sense that he hurt her and abandoned

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:12.080
her in some way, causing her to fall into
a deep depression and replay the idea she

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.500
has in her head of when they would see each
other again.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:17.180
This idea is supported by the fact that she
starts laughing.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:21.729
That leads me to believe that in her head,
Gerald responded to her and said something

00:05:21.729 --> 00:05:22.889
that she found funny.

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:26.360
This would also kind of explain why she was
waiting in the hotel room and came out when

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:27.360
she saw me.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.510
It wouldn’t be so different from when you
see a dog waiting by the window for their

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:31.949
master to return.

00:05:31.949 --> 00:05:36.139
If she truly did have some kind of traumatic
experience with Gerald, it’s possible that

00:05:36.139 --> 00:05:38.669
this was just her way of dealing with.

00:05:38.669 --> 00:05:43.640
I’m no expert on the human brain, but if
we do go with the story about the woman and

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:44.640
Gerald…

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:48.530
I shudder to think about what may have caused
her to get kicked out of the hotel and the

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:49.530
cops called.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:54.259
I really have nothing to go on here, but my
gut tells me that her perceived reunion with

00:05:54.259 --> 00:05:58.849
Gerald may not have gone that well and possibly
brought up some repressed scars.

00:05:58.849 --> 00:06:03.889
Again, I have no actual idea what went down,
but I imagine a delusional old woman screaming

00:06:03.889 --> 00:06:07.770
and crying at an unseen presence in the middle
of the hall one night would have scared some

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:09.630
of the hotel guests and staff.

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:13.960
The fact that she was removed from the room
tells me that she may have even gotten violent

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:15.360
towards one of the other guests.

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:20.420
If me simply walking by was enough to trigger
delusions of the past, imagine what danger

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:24.729
someone trying to calm her down might have
been in.

00:06:24.729 --> 00:06:28.750
That’s it for this episode of True Fear,
but you won’t want to miss out on the next

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:34.430
one, where I’ll be telling you about the
gunman on my subway train.

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:38.530
This is going to be the most intense episode
yet, and I actually have some pretty scary

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:40.939
raw footage of what went on that day.

00:06:40.939 --> 00:06:44.180
So if you don’t want to miss it be sure
to subscribe to CZsWorld.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:49.129
We’ve got new horrors every other week so
ring that death bell for notifications and

00:06:49.129 --> 00:06:51.300
I’ll see you in the next one.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.620
Assuming, we both survive.

